WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.225
Hi, friends. This is The Ripple.

00:00:12.225 --> 00:00:16.449
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:18.984
Hands flat on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:18.984 --> 00:00:21.519
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:21.519 --> 00:00:29.124
Drop a pebble in water, and rings spread out, one ring touching the next.

00:00:29.124 --> 00:00:37.573
Kind and calm acts are like that. One small act touches something, and that touches something else.

00:00:37.573 --> 00:00:45.178
Today we follow your ripple — your own small act, and where it travels.

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:51.937
Pretend with me. Your friend needs the red crayon, and you pass it over.

00:00:51.937 --> 00:00:57.852
That is the pebble. Small, and yours. Watch the first ring.

00:00:57.852 --> 00:01:03.766
Your friend finishes their picture. Their shoulders relax. They feel proud.

00:01:03.766 --> 00:01:09.681
Second ring: they show the picture, and it makes your teacher smile.

00:01:09.681 --> 00:01:13.906
Third ring: the whole table feels a little calmer. One crayon did all that traveling.

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:20.665
One more. A pretend classmate drops their pencils — pencils everywhere.

00:01:20.665 --> 00:01:26.580
You kneel down and help pick them up. That is your pebble this time.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:32.495
First ring: their worry melts. Second ring: they hold the door for someone else, later.

00:01:32.495 --> 00:01:37.564
Nobody counted your rings. A ripple is for noticing, not for keeping score.

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:44.324
One small act. Watch what it touches. Watch what that touches. That is The Ripple.

00:01:44.324 --> 00:01:50.238
Your next kind act is already a pebble, waiting in your hand.

00:01:50.238 --> 00:01:56.153
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:01:56.153 --> 00:01:59.533
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:01:59.533 --> 00:02:02.913
You're ready for what's next.
